---
import LofiLayout from '../../layouts/LofiLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../../lib/base';
---

<LofiLayout title="About">
  <p class="muted"><a href={withBase('/lofi')}>&larr; home</a></p>
  <h1>We are Brink</h1>
  <p>
    A global team of technologists, designers, strategists and behavioural
    scientists. We apply a method we call Behavioural Innovation to solve big
    problems in ways that take human behaviour into account.
  </p>
  <p>
    We work with people who are frustrated by the status quo and ready to take
    on the world's most pressing challenges: funders building new models,
    changemakers seeking fresh approaches, and leaders future-proofing their
    institutions. We're now part of Africa Practice.
  </p>

  <h2>Behavioural Innovation</h2>
  <p>
    We combine the behavioural sciences with innovation methods to deliver
    lasting impact, drawing on psychology, anthropology, sociology and economics
    to build the mindsets and mechanisms that shift systems.
  </p>
  <p>True innovation happens when we:</p>
  <ul class="plain">
    <li>Put people at the centre, because the real world has real people in it</li>
    <li>Use insights into how people think and act to fuel breakthrough ideas</li>
    <li>Deeply understand incentives, to shift systems</li>
    <li>Treat transforming mindset as seriously as developing skillset</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Our team</h2>
  <p>
    From London to Kigali, Barcelona to Nairobi, our thinkers and doers
    collaborate across borders, tackling complex challenges and driving
    meaningful change worldwide. Diversity is in our DNA: it means working in
    multidisciplinary ways, and articulating a more global perspective on
    innovation that reflects the innovators we work with.
  </p>

  <h2>More</h2>
  <ul class="plain">
    <li><a href={withBase('/lofi/our-work')}>Our work</a></li>
    <li><a href={withBase('/lofi/blog')}>Blog</a></li>
    <li><a href={withBase('/behavioural-innovation')}>Behavioural Innovation (full site)</a></li>
  </ul>
</LofiLayout>
